{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790262693,"nonce":"USH9eIxtL5h7K3UZREQ4Lv6zDjk=","title":"Lua: require(\"name\") followed by a field or call is not seen as a file of the program","message":"The scope pass records a require only when the call is the whole expression (`require \"m\"`, `require(\"m\")`). `require(\"m\").f` or `require(\"m\")(x)` records nothing: the file is not loaded with the program and dynamic_globals stays off, so a global the module sets is not seen by the main chunk.\n\n    -- modg.lua\n    shared_g = 41\n    return {f = function() return shared_g + 1 end}\n    -- main.lua\n    local f = require(\"modg\").f\n    print(f(), shared_g)\n\nlua5.4 prints \"42 41\"; zylua (main dea6d08b) prints \"42 nil\". Recording the literal name for a require call followed by further suffixes would fix it.","files":null}]}